Assignment 16: Lambda Function Optimization and Cost Analysis
Task:
Optimize Lambda function for performance and cost.
What to Do:
●    Create Lambda function that:
●    Reads 1000 objects from S3
●    Processes JSON data
●    Writes results to DynamoDB
●    Initially use 128MB memory
●    Use Lambda Power Tuning tool or manual testing:
●    Test with 128MB, 256MB, 512MB, 1024MB
●    Measure execution time and cost
●    Find optimal configuration
●    Optimize code:
●    Add connection pooling
●    Implement batch writes to DynamoDB
●    Use async operations
●    Compare performance:
●    Before optimization vs after
●    Different memory sizes
●    Enable X-Ray tracing
●    Analyze cold start vs warm start times
●    Implement Lambda@Edge concept (if time allows)
Success Criteria:
●    Identify cost-optimal memory size
●    Cold start < 3 seconds
●    Warm execution < 1 second